<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Entitlements for the macOS bundle, applied when Tauri signs it. Referenced by
  `bundle.macOS.entitlements` in `tauri.conf.json`.

  Deliberately empty. The full app carries
  `com.apple.security.device.audio-input`, because it records; this one never
  does — `hanzi-voice` is built with `default-features = false`, so its capture
  half and `cpal` are not linked, and `Info.ios.plist` has no microphone string
  for the same reason. The key was copied across all the same and is gone since
  issue #41: an entitlement the binary has no use for is one a reviewer asks
  about. `tests/ipc_contract.rs` checks the two stay in step; if this app ever
  records, the key comes back with `NSMicrophoneUsageDescription`, or capture
  returns silence in the signed bundle.

  `com.apple.security.app-sandbox` is deliberately absent. The full app has
  since turned the sandbox on for its Mac App Store build (its Entitlements.plist
  has the history); this app has not, and that is a decision of its own to take
  rather than one to make as a side effect of a microphone or file change.

  Unlike the full app, this one would not need
  `com.apple.security.files.user-selected.read-write` if it were sandboxed: it
  shows no save or open panel and reads or writes no file the learner picks.
  Add that key alongside the sandbox if that ever changes.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
</dict>
</plist>
